    "recommendations": "Providing a clearly marked address visible from the street and at the driveway entrance could significantly improve response times given the single access point and extended driveway length. Ensuring the driveway remains wide enough to accommodate emergency vehicles and allows for turnaround or staging near the main building would support effective operations, particularly where rear access is limited. Keeping the driveway and any pathways between the main building and detached structure clear of encroaching vegetation could improve both navigation and aerial visibility for responding personnel. A secondary egress path, where feasible within the property, may further enhance responder and occupant movement options during an emergency."
